  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\n\r\n36683 BGR A1 XX DR AT 001 P04, 36683 BGL A1 XX DR AT 001 PL02, 36683 BGR A1 XX DR AT 002 P06, G623-LSV-XX-XX-DR-S-1003 Rev P01, Design and Access Statement prepared by Baily Garner, Tree Survey and Schedule of Trees prepared by Places for People, Arboricultural Method Statement prepared by Places for People, Arboricultural Method Statement, Tree Protection Plan and Tree Constraints Plan prepared by e3p.\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those of the existing building, unless otherwise specified in the approved application. \r\n\r\nReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area in accordance with the requirements of policies D1 and D2 of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017. \r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed and working practices adopted in accordance with the document entitled Arboricultural Method Statement & Tree Protection Plan dated 28 August 2026, prepared by E3P, reference 70-189. All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report.\r\n \r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan."
  ],
